## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to translate a compliance feature into a concrete, time-bound cost-benefit analysis suitable for a beginner. It tests how assumptions drive ROI and how to articulate go/no-go criteria.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation basics for small features
- ROI calculation and break-even timing
- Risk penalties avoided and adoption uplift
- Simple, testable calculations and trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
function breakEvenMonths(laborRatePerHr, weeks, engineers, monthlyOverhead, annualBenefit) {
  const upfront = laborRatePerHr * weeks * engineers * 40;
  const monthlyBenefit = annualBenefit / 12;
  const netMonthlyBenefit = monthlyBenefit - monthlyOverhead;
  if (netMonthlyBenefit <= 0) return Infinity;
  return Math.ceil(upfront / netMonthlyBenefit);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust for ARR vs one-time benefits?
- What metrics would you track after launch to validate forecasts?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to reason about on-device ML tradeoffs, privacy, federated updates, and cost implications for a beginner-level feature in widely-used apps.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference and model sizing
- Federated learning basics and backend costs
- Energy and latency budgets for mobile feeds
- Privacy/compliance and user consent flows
- Rollout strategies and offline fallback
- Drift/maintenance and break-even horizon

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-cost estimator (not used in production)
function estimateCBA(modelMB, latencyMs, energyPerInference, users) {
  const deviceCost = modelMB * 1.2;
  const latencyCost = latencyMs * 0.5;
  const energyCost = energyPerInference * 60;
  const backendCost = 0.1;
  return deviceCost + latencyCost + energyCost + backendCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you estimate user consent overhead in practice?
- What metrics signal drift in a deployed on-device ranking model?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes a candidate's ability to quantify costs for an on-device feature with privacy constraints and optional cloud lifts, focusing on edge-cases and governance.

## Key Concepts
- On-device storage budgeting
- Edge compute energy budget
- Privacy/compliance & consent overhead
- Rollout strategy and drift maintenance

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost(storageMB, cpuW, users, cloudPerUser) {
  const storageCost = storageMB * 0.01;
  const energyCost = cpuW * 24 * 365 * 0.0003;
  const telemetry = users * cloudPerUser;
  return storageCost + energyCost + telemetry;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the break-even horizon with real usage data?
- What safeguards would you implement for data minimization and consent revocation?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses cost-aware design of privacy-preserving observability with edge processing, cross-region deployment, and go/no-go decisions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge compute budgeting
- Privacy-first telemetry
- Data retention and regional regulations
- Multi-region cost models
- Rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function cba(params) {
  // simple cost model
  const deviceCost = params.deviceCPU * 0.1 + params.deviceMem * 0.05;
  const deltaCost = (params.deltaKB / 1024) * 0.02;
  const centralCost = params.retentionMonths * 1000 * 0.01;
  return deviceCost + deltaCost + centralCost;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for GDPR/CCPA across regions?
- What metrics would tie cost to business value beyond raw savings?
